t(1, 740, """Breaking the laws of physics is real; but beware of misunderstanding it, for in that lies ruin

Over the past months a small number of the brothers who write to me privately, and a few of the commenters, raised questions about physical wonders and asked me to speak on matters I do not much like to delve into, because one who has not experienced will not grasp it .. his mind will not bear it .. Physical wonders, though they are an existing reality in which we believe with full and complete faith, definitely and categorically do not belong to the grave-worshippers. Every worshipper of a grave and every keeper of a tomb is a dajjal for whom nothing of the law of physics is broken; rather he babbles to people, play-acts, lies and deceives.

Even so, I will speak about physical wonders for a very important purpose, to me the most important purpose of all .. The purpose is that we believe and are certain that Allah Most High is able to do all things with the certainty of the eyewitness who sees with his heart and his eye, not the certainty of a mind built on transmitted text alone. The transmitted text (the Book of Allah Most High) only takes hold of the heart and eye through seeing and witnessing fact and reality. Although ((most)) people know this by word of mouth and by reciting the Book of Allah, many souls turn away from certainty in it in heart, soul and spirit, or are indifferent to it, or find it hard!

As for the breaking of the laws and of physics, it is established by an explicit text in the Book of our Great Lord, for humans and not for jinn, in the story of Asif ibn Barkhiya, may Allah be pleased with him, the companion who sat with Allah's prophet Sulayman, peace be upon him, when he brought Allah's prophet Sulayman the throne of Bilqis. It was the throne itself, not a copy of it nor an image of it .. He brought it to him without moving from his place, that is, Asif .. He brought a very tangible body, of wood and many other touchable, tangible, manufactured materials that the hand can touch, hold and feel .. He brought it from Yemen to Palestine in a fraction of a second or the blink of an eye, so the throne was truly gone from the king's palace in Yemen and its place became empty.

The one who did that was a righteous man of the sons of Adam, peace be upon him; not a jinni, nor a marid, nor an ifrit. Therefore the breaking of the law is established and confirmed by the text of the Book of Allah the Great, our Lord, the Able, the Giver, the Subduer (He subdues physics and the laws of the universe).

The problem is not our all believing in this truth with complete faith. The problem is the dajjals' use of this faith and this knowledge of faith among a number of Muslims in order to pretend that they do what Asif ibn Barkhiya did. This is something not to be accepted, and it cannot be accepted by believing it, because in it is a great trial for people and an invitation to corrupt the hearts of the ignorant among them, who then think the wali is a prophet and messenger; indeed some of them have worshipped the awliya, prostrated to them and prostrated to their graves without any karamat, but upon lies and deceit. So what if the true awliya - and they are real on earth, not a lie - were made known .. what if they announced their karamat, which need not be of the kind of moving matter from one place to another.

As for the one who asks me whether there can be, in the creation of Allah the Great and among His servants, in our time or in any time, someone who moves matter as Asif ibn Barkhiya did, or even moves himself, I say: definitely possible, and very possible, and I find no problem in that, on a fixed rule that does not change: Allah is able to do all things. But I do not believe the words of any person who comes and tells me, I do such and such, of what breaks the physical nature of the laws of the earth .. A claim like this does not concern me; I do not accept it, nor does anyone else. So our problem is with the claim, not with the truth and reality that the matter is very possible, and there is never a problem in its happening, because the moving of tangible matter is established in the Book of our Lord. And just as our Lord is definitely and certainly able to enable a human to move non-living, inanimate matter, so our Lord, the Able, the Great, is definitely and certainly able to enable any of His creation to move himself, with his living matter.

As for me, I was asked, and I answered that nothing like transfer or moving has happened to me; rather I have witnessed other matters and cases in which the laws are broken completely .. As for what relates to transfer, one day I wished in my heart to see what transfer means and how it feels .. That was months ago. I saw a dream in which I saw myself in a place on a highway and suddenly I was transferred into a city, and I felt the transfer in the dream .. the transfer of the body .. But without the body coming apart, and it did not move as parts; rather it moves with complete lightness, as if the matter is the blink of an eye: you are in a place and you come to be in a place. This was an experience in a dream, not in reality.

And my last advice before I conclude ..""")

t(2, 75, """The relationship with heaven .. the relationship with the Lord of heaven and the Lord of the whole universe, hallowed be His names .. then with what He shows His servants if He wills; it is a relationship not built by seeking wonders and striving after them .. That means you are not worshipping Allah .. you do that so that wonders happen to you .. then you are not worshipping Allah .. then Allah Most High does not matter to you and is not in your heart nor in your soul; you have an aim and an interest, and your goal is not Allah Most High! What worship is this? The occurrence of wonders that break physics is a result; you do not seek them at all, do not think of them, and they never cross your mind when you truly worship Allah with real worship and are occupied with Him alone. So everyone who prayed for wonders at the start of his commitment has not worshipped Allah. But asking for a wonder is understandable when your relationship with Allah Most High has become excellent and there is a reason for asking it, not merely to obtain it; and when you obtain it you do not broadcast it or tell people of it, and it stays only between you and Allah Most High. This requires that you yourself have moved to the world of the spirit, not that you are immersed in wronging people and in desires, pray 10 thousand rak'ahs a day and say, I want karamat .. Then you want deceit, not a witnessing by which your heart is made firm so that you are helped, by the permission of the Most Merciful, on the hard and lonely road. For it is indeed lonely and hard, and you may face a very great challenge on earth, as if the world were shut upon you, so you ask Allah Most High for the breaking of physics; not a request for high rank, but the request of one in dire need! And we do not believe any person who comes and says, I move from place to place, because this is a door of great trial for people; we block it at once before giving any chance at all for it to open, and we reject it from the root, completely and decisively .. This is the method.

In conclusion, we never, ever worship Allah Most High, hallowed be His names, so that He breaks something for us. It is enough for us to live worshipping Him, by His favour and grace upon us, with a good, guided worship to which He guides us as a favour from Him, and to die without any wonders or breaches of physics; that does not matter. For we do ((not)) worship Allah Most High for interests on earth, nor to tell and recount stories of what happened to us, nor to talk of details. We worship our Great Lord only for Him, in Him and for His sake, and this is what must occupy us 24 hours/24 hours, and nothing else.""")

t(2, 1095, """It set out from Ethiopia .. covered the west of Yemen, then turned toward the sea before reaching the east of Yemen and the Sultanate of Oman, then reached India and covered parts of it! This is a clear message .. to those who fear punishments on earth and from heaven .. The message is: Allah Most High is the Owner of everything. He says to the wind: send the ash to that place and keep it away from that place .. Or He commands the volcanic ash itself, without any wind or air, and says to it: keep away from that place and cover that place .. Many people (not all) think that Allah Most High needs wind to remove a danger, or something of the means of His earth! When I lay on the hospital bed for 17 days in 2021 I saw Him, hallowed be His names .. I saw Him with my heart .. And I still, and today is 2025 .. I still feel the very same terror .. the terror at the reality of His power .. His power that no mind can imagine .. His power, His majesty and the reality of His Essence; hallowed be all His names and attributes .. Exalted .. exalted .. magnified .. magnified .. hallowed above His heavens and His earth and above His universes, whose number and nature none knows but He .. Hallowed and magnified above what He created, of what our minds conceive and of what is impossible to conceive at all .. When He wills a thing it happens and comes about without a cause .. And when He wills a karamah for His righteous servants on His earth, He places in the hearts of the men and the women a supplication; they utter it and He answers them, as a karamah for them .. He wills what He wills .. does what He wills .. chooses what He wills .. Magnify the Lord""")

t(3, 115, """If you are told the whole world has gone up in flames .. be with Allah the Great, our Lord .. taking the means after, not before, turning to Allah Most High .. Months ago I saw a dream of glad tidings for people .. I saw that I was in a ground-floor house, not my present house .. and I was sitting on a prayer rug throughout the dream, praying and supplicating. Then outside the house very strong explosions took place; I saw them while I was inside the house on the prayer rug, without going outside. So I prostrated to Allah the Great, our Lord, the Most Merciful, for a time in the dream, then I rose from prostration and the explosions stopped, and I actually went outside in the dream and found, in place of the fires and destruction, roses, crops and a gentle shining sun, and the people in the street happy and joyful, as if nothing had happened or taken place.""")

t(3, 1430, """The amount of fatigue, pain, affliction, strain, toil and exhaustion that you may pay from your blood, your soul, your spirit and from everything your mind imagines and does not imagine, if you decide to hold to justice in your personal life and say: No .. I will not wrong anyone; it is an amount of psychological and bodily aches and pains of which the least that can be said is that they are a painful torment, an abiding blaze and great agonies. Many people tire of paying the price at its start, so they retreat and change their deeds from justice to injustice, tired from the first of the road and its beginning, and they relapse .. Some fall and relapse in the middle of the road, having wasted all the effort, and weariness has overtaken them .. And some hold firm by the power of Allah the Great, not by their own power or strength.

The scale of justice is the hardest .. the most difficult .. and the greatest cause of fatigue and exhaustion in the life of this world .. When the world .. and people .. and everything join against you .. and none has mercy on you but Allah .. and the mercy of people is stripped from your path for long years, so they tear at you and chew your flesh, your soul and your spirit without stopping .. When that befalls you because you were told: do wrong .. and you said, I will not .. and the world attacked you like a raging wind .. then you are in the greatest test of all!""")

t(4, 475, """Tap on the pictures""")

t(4, 1570, """Questions come to me about people who tell others that the first of the signs to appear is the rising of the sun from the west, and they cite a hadith that mentions this. The detail in this matter is very long, but in brief .. The following hadith is also authentic, in Sahih Muslim: The Prophet ﷺ said: "Hasten to good deeds before six: the Dajjal, the Smoke, the Beast of the earth, the rising of the sun from its west, the affair of the general public, and the private affair of each one of you." [Narrated by Muslim: 2947].

To avoid length .. The rising of the sun from its west means the final closing of the door of repentance, and this fits with the emergence of the Beast that marks people as believer and disbeliever .. As for saying that the first of the signs is the rising of the sun from its west, it is a grave and great error, in the understanding, not in the wording of the hadith that says so .. Because the door of repentance will not close,,,, will not close,,,, ever ..
As long as the tests on earth have not yet ended!
The Mahdi is a test and trial for Muslims and non-Muslims
The Great Battle is a test and trial for Muslims
The Dajjal is a test and trial for all mankind
Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him, is a test for the Christians

Therefore, the sun will never, absolutely never, rise from its west as long as these tests have not yet ended

My words end here .. I am the servant in need of Allah Most High .. But whoever would like more, from the words of the scholars of the Salaf, among the greatest scholars of the Ummah, here is the following:

Ibn Hajar said in al-Fath: What is preponderant from the sum of the reports is that the emergence of the Dajjal is the first of the great signs announcing the change of general conditions over most of the earth, and that the rising of the sun from the west is the first of the great signs announcing the change of the conditions of the upper world. Perhaps the emergence of the Beast occurs on the same day on which the sun rises from the west... Al-Hakim said: What appears is that the rising of the sun precedes the emergence of the Beast, then the Beast emerges on that day or the one near it. End.

Al-Mubarakfuri said in the commentary on al-Tirmidhi: Know that the narrations differ on the order of the ten signs, and so the people of knowledge differed on their order. It was said that the first of the signs is the Smoke, then the emergence of the Dajjal, then the descent of Isa, peace be upon him, then""")

t(5, 45, """the emergence of Ya'juj and Ma'juj, then the emergence of the Beast, then the rising of the sun from its west. For the disbelievers accept Islam in the time of Isa, peace be upon him, until the call becomes one; and had the sun risen from its west before the emergence of the Dajjal and his descent, faith would not be accepted from the disbelievers. The "and" is for mere conjunction, so it is no objection that his descent is before its rising, nor that it is reported that the rising of the sun is the first of the signs... End.

As for the hadith of Muslim from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: I memorised from the Messenger of Allah, saying: "The first of the signs to appear are the rising of the sun from its west and the emergence of the Beast upon the people in the forenoon; whichever of them comes before its companion, the other follows close on its heels." The author of Awn al-Ma'bud said of it: Some explained the firstness in this hadith thus: the signs are either tokens indicating the nearness of the Hour or indicating its coming to be. Of the first are the Dajjal and the like; of the second are the rising of the sun and the like. So the firstness of the rising of the sun is only in relation to the second category. End.

As for the hadith "Three, when they emerge", it does not contradict what we mentioned of the firstness of the emergence of the Dajjal, because the conjunction in the hadith is by "and", which does not require order; by it the earlier may be joined to the later and the reverse.. As in His saying, Most High: "He has ordained for you of religion what He enjoined on Nuh, and what We revealed to you, and what We enjoined on Ibrahim, Musa and Isa: establish the religion and do not be divided in it. Hard upon the polytheists is that to which you call them. Allah chooses for Himself whom He wills and guides to Himself whoever turns to Him." {Al-Shura: 13}.""")

t(5, 860, """To the brothers asking here in the comments about the volcanic cloud in the Sultanate of Oman .. Allah the Great, our Lord, has shown favour by decreeing that the cloud veer to the Arabian Sea; it is over the sea, heading to the south of Pakistan and the north of India. It did not reach the Sultanate of Oman at all, praise be to Allah.""")

t(5, 1165, """Another, different world is coming, by Allah's permission""")

t(5, 2255, """O noble ones .. Hardly a day passes me without my watching images of the world and the cities 150 years ago .. I watch the people .. the streets.. People rushing to their work .. people practising their trades .. people eating.. people rejoicing .. marrying.. riding buses.. riding animals .. Every person living his reality .. his life .. his chance .. Then they died .. they all died .. This means that we too will die.. like them.. What does this mean? It means our story will end just as their story ended! So what is it that people wrestle over? They wrong and harm and do not fear their Lord? Everyone's stories will end.. as the previous stories ended .. Then we will become a memory as they became a memory.. All of us will become a memory .. something that passed and went .. Those who live after us will say: so-and-so lived and died .. so-and-so, a woman, lived and died .. They did not remember this end, except those who remembered .. Look at the picture of these dead! They had life projects .. They went out in the morning to work .. married.. had children .. celebrated.. bought and sold .. lived life to the full.. as if they would not die ..""")

t(6, 45, """as if they would not depart .. People today also think (most of them) that the moment of their departure will not come .. busy with the movement of life.. with its pulling them along .. Have they not heard it said: so-and-so died on his wedding night .. so-and-so suddenly fell ill and died .. so-and-so suddenly went and departed .. Not stopping is a mistake .. and rushing headlong is a mistake .. One must remember every day .. Remembering is salvation.. Remembering the Hereafter is wisdom .. intelligence .. discernment .. and the best daily deed in rank with the Great Lord after worship""")

t(6, 1330, """Building a house in hours!""")

t(6, 2390, """For the attention of the brothers and sisters who follow the recitation broadcast on the channel: unfortunately the broadcasting of more recitation will stop and we will make do with what is on the channel, because the state of exhaustion, fatigue and choking and the visual effect on the vowel marks have increased and become tiring and exhausting, growing ever greater and not stopping at a set level .. Tonight's recitation was not recorded, and things were better, by the favour and grace of Allah Most High: no choking and no difficulty in reciting as happens when recording. We ask Allah Most High for blessing and benefit in what has been published .. and we ask Allah the Great, our Lord, for relief for us all, if Allah wills.""")

t(7, 305, """Just hours before the Ethiopia volcano I wrote here: Divine punishments are of many kinds; they are not confined to the sign of the Smoke. Man narrows what is wide in the will of Allah .. The earth is full of volcanoes able to bring down empires; a sea that rages for seven days, or for 7 minutes, or for a fraction of a second, by the power of Allah, which has nothing to do with physics, and takes everything in its path; a rain rained upon them that spares nothing and leaves nothing .. The Ethiopia volcano is a reminder to those who thought that the power of Allah is confined only to the sign of the Smoke, that He cannot destroy a wrongdoer except by one of the ten major signs, and cannot establish truth on earth except by one of the ten major signs! The reply came: a volcano and smoke from the earth, not from the sky.
As for our Lord's saying about the earth, when it takes on its adornment, that the command of Allah comes to it (Our command came to it), ijtihad is open to reflecting that Our command is the sign of the Smoke; but (Our command) has recurred many times in human history and was not the sign of the Smoke even once among those times! Because Allah the Great, our Lord, sent down numerous punishments on the people of the earth over thousands of years, and not a single punishment among them was a major sign; the major signs were stored away, by the decree of Allah Most High, for the events of the end of the earth.

As for the ten major signs, they are not a sign of the end of great powers. Allah Most High brought down the Roman Empire, the superpower of its time, by a mouse, not even by a volcano .. So the ten major signs, the Smoke among them, are not for bringing down great powers when they do wrong. Rather the ten major signs are beads strung in succession, having the quality of following one another, to prepare the people of the earth for the Day of Resurrection. They are religious signs for the sake of religion, not for the sake of smashing great powers .. The Smoke is for the sake of religion because it is linked to the Dajjal, Judaism, Christianity and Islam. The rising of the sun from the west is linked to religion because it is the closing of the door of repentance. The Beast relates to religion because it marks the believer and the disbeliever. The three sinkings of the earth relate to religion because through them the establishment of the true religion begins. The fire that gathers people gathers them for the Day of Religion. The Dajjal emerges in an emergence relating to religion. The descent of Allah's prophet Isa is for the sake of religion. Ya'juj and Ma'juj are a sign for ending wars on the face of the earth entirely, for the sake of religion, so that Allah's prophet Isa and the Muslims may enjoy practising their religion until the death of Allah's prophet Isa without danger or wars, and so that religious wars end among mankind. For Ya'juj and Ma'juj emerge fighting for their atheist creed, and atheism is one of the forms of belief. They say, that is Ya'juj and Ma'juj, when they reach Lake Tiberias and find no one: we have killed the people of the earth, so let us kill the people of heaven, mocking and jeering. This shows that they are atheists; had they believed in the existence of a god they would not have said what they said. So their emergence is not political or military; it is an emergence to kill every believing man and woman on earth. Thus their sign is a major one that also relates to religion and to their creed of atheism. And to magnify a great power in the soul, so that a person thinks it a superpower to the degree that our Great Lord cannot bring it down except by a major sign - this, by Allah, is a great lack of understanding of Allah Most High and of His ways on earth, and it is of the error of magnifying the powers of humans in the soul and deeming them very strong on the scale of the power of Allah the Great.

Our Great Lord, hallowed be His names, says of the wording, Our command came, in a place where there is no sign of the ten major signs:
﴿Until, when Our command came and the oven gushed forth, We said: "Load into it of every kind a pair, two, and your family - except those against whom the word has already gone forth - and those who believe." And none believed with him but a few﴾""")

t(7, 1770, """Some brothers in private think that I have abundant knowledge on one of the topics most discussed among Muslims today. Their questions are not a crime and their interest in this topic is not a mistake, but I am not the one fit to answer them on this matter .. Questions reach me in private about the Imam Mahdi .. I would like to say that the servant in need of Allah does not know the unseen; none knows the unseen but Allah Most High. And to make clear the reality of things, how there is no person on earth who encompasses everything, and that we shift between an ignorance and a knowledge: I did not know what the Imam Mahdi means, in his very simple basic details, except from my first wife. She is the one who acquainted me with the basic details that people know and that I was ignorant of, and that was at the age of perhaps 23 .. So to the brothers who write to me, may Allah protect them: you are asking a person who knew nothing of the Imam Mahdi but his title, and only in his early youth. So do not rely much on my possibly knowing a lot of information about him. Were it not for Allah's covering of us .. And I contemplate Allah's covering and recall my ignorance, in my early youth, of the obvious things people know about the events of the end of time, and my 100% heedlessness of them, until she whom Allah willed to teach me then taught me .. So the Imam is hidden in the breasts and in the understandings, and in that whose realities none knows except those whom Allah taught and for whom He willed that.""")

t(7, 2390, """And a reminder .. On WhatsApp; a note that is hard for me to send to those in contact one by one .. one by one, to those who got in touch and multiplied the titles .. and searching among the WhatsApp messages one by one is exhausting.

O noble ones .. I am not a sheikh, for sheikh means scholar, and I have not studied Islamic knowledge apart from readings .. I am not an ustadh .. I am not a doctor, even though I hold higher degrees .. Even if a Muslim came to me one day and said to me: a voice came to me""")

t(8, 60, """from heaven and said to him: tell Doctor Faraj such and such .. For heaven may send what it sends; that is an outpouring of the mercies of the Great Lord, His favour and His generosity .. But we, here on earth, are watched for what we do with what comes to us .. and how we behave with what is opened to us .. And there is no harm in an example being set .. We strive to make the model, and our reward is with Allah Most High .. Then, I am not a sayyid .. I am not, I am not

O noble ones .. Know that titles are like a throne in the heart, and no human on earth ought to have a throne in his heart ..

Then, this is what I hope, by Allah, for every believing man and woman and every Muslim man and woman: if every person were to meet Allah's prophet Muhammad and Allah's prophet Isa, blessings and peace be upon them both, and Allah Most High unveiled for him the sight of their two beautiful hearts, he would realise that the greatest blessing after Islam is the blessing of understanding the truth .. Your brother passed through many, different, varied and numerous stations of truth until I understood .. And when I understood I was never again as I had been .. And when I understood I was thunderstruck by the truth of the truth .. and by the unveiling of the truth .. Then that was crowned by the model of two noble prophets among those of firm resolve, whose hearts are more, and more, and more innocent than the heart of a child just born .. So when I saw that with the sight of certainty .. and knew it with a knowledge that falsehood and doubt cannot approach from before it or from behind it, and witnessed it with a witnessing by which the proof of witnessing is established against the one given it, not to be consoled or comforted but to be held to account and punished .. When that happened to me I understood, realised and was freed .. freed from the illusions in which people are drowning .. from the nonsense into which people have fallen .. and from the names and titles in which people are lost because they adopted them .. So I am only brother Faraj, or only brother Omar, or Abu Muhammad .. or Faraj with nothing else, or Omar with nothing else .. All that is true and right, and titles other than that are illusion, deception and distancing from the truth .. The truth is what I saw in the hearts of Allah's two prophets Muhammad and Isa, blessings and peace be upon them both. That is the beautiful truth .. the truth that comforts the spirit .. the truth that, by Allah, is higher than a thousand thousand titles .. and than a thousand thousand professorships and doctorates .. the truth of the divine blessing .. the blessing of a person seeing himself as one of the people .. of them and with them .. How many millions and millions of ustadhs, doctors and professors are there? Millions and millions .. But Muhammad ﷺ is only one person .. and Isa, peace be upon him, is only one person .. and Musa, peace be upon him, is only one person .. I think the reader will now understand well what I saw in the hearts of Allah's two noble prophets Muhammad and Isa, blessings and peace be upon them both .. and will understand that the truth is in their hearts, not in thrones set up inside hearts .. nor in titles by which the soul grows grand, puffs up and swells .. So I ask Allah Most High, for every believing man and woman, for our offspring, our neighbours, our wives and all believing husbands, the like of this that I am speaking of; by Allah it is great, but most people do not know.""")

t(8, 1385, """Please concentrate on what I am about to explain .. Unfortunately there is a great deal of mistaken understanding among many people about a matter that is at the core of mankind's coming future

The Prophet ﷺ said to Ibn Sayyad: "I have hidden something for you." He said: "The Dukh." He said: "Away with you! You will never exceed your measure." Umar said: "Permit me to strike his neck." He said: "Leave him; if it is he, you will not be able to overcome him, and if it is not he, there is no good for you in killing him."
Summary of the hadith scholar's ruling: [Authentic]
Narrator: Abdullah ibn Umar | Hadith scholar: al-Bukhari | Source: Sahih al-Bukhari

The Dajjal, in his dialogue with the Prophet ﷺ through the body of Ibn Sayyad, the curse be upon him, belittled the sign of the Smoke. So why did he belittle it? Because the sign of the Smoke does not affect his abilities of wonders .. Wonders, not miracles .. Miracles are for the prophets .. karamat for the awliya .. and wonders for the dajjals; even if he were a small dajjal in a village, what he brings with the help of the disbelieving jinn is wonders.
The Dajjal has wonders, so the sign of the Smoke does not stop his wonders; that is why he tried to make a diminutive of the word (Dukhan) and said (Dukh). So the Prophet ﷺ became angry, and al-Faruq, may Allah be pleased with him, who was present at the scene with the Prophet ﷺ, became angry at him.

So we have learned why the Dajjal sees no danger to himself in the sign of the Smoke. The answer is that he has wonders; and it is not correct, as some of our brothers and sisters think, that he needs electricity because he will ride a plane .. and will make a hologram using electricity and broadcast it in the sky .. All this is incorrect .. The Dajjal, when he makes his clear, complete emergence, in which lie his death and his end, will use the wonders of the devils of the jinn; the door of that will be opened for him and he will be permitted it, so that the test takes place on earth .. But his anger at the sign of the Smoke is not because it affects him directly; rather because it affects the West, which has enjoyed the civilisation of electricity for centuries, and the return of the world to before smart technology, that is, to the mechanical state: such as the pistol, gunpowder and rifles that work by the spark of gunpowder, and advanced bullets made even under the stairs in some regions of Pakistan, needing no electricity to fill them with gunpowder; and the shift of weaponry from satellites to gunpowder alone, the firing of the remaining missiles on the field of the battles of the Great Battle without electricity, and the equalising of military power between the Muslims and the Romans, who have defended his project for hundreds of years so that he would not be forced to make his complete emergence, which he never wants because he knows its end .. This is what will anger him. Because the new victors will come very close to his place, and he will turn into the heir of the defeat of a nation on which he long relied .. Among them he will turn into one defeated, weak, wretched and broken, because their technological power, which will have ended, fallen and collapsed, was always the important psychological bond that tied them to him and made them loyal to him. So when the sign of the Smoke comes and their civilisation ends entirely (almost), what is left for them of him to be loyal to him for? He will then see that the bond of interest between the Romans and him has fallen .. Nothing will remain for him but one thing to stop the bleeding of his loss of the Romans, which is to make his emergence, which has nothing to do with the laws of physics, nor with electricity, nor with reason and logic, from near or far, as many think .. The cause of the anger is that the relationship between him and the Romans will have collapsed and his small state in the Middle East collapsed, and all his effort of thousands of years gone to dust .. So the harm that will anger him is a harm""")
